"""Release Reaction, Layer 2 (why): the factor register. The full research universe (the 77 items of the ChatGPT list that Rich shared on 2026-10-26, grouped A to I),
each marked with what the repo holds for it. Status is the author's reading of what is on disk or on the sheet; where a source was checked it is named, otherwise the status is stated as an assumption.
Statuses:
  sheet     measured and on the going-in factor sheet (known before the release, point in time)
  data      data exists in the repo (or is fetchable) but is not on the sheet yet
  partial   only a proxy or a thin / short record exists
  missing   no data for it here
  noobs     not observable with data of this kind (no order book, no stop locations)
  after     a label read from the reaction AFTER the release (Layer 2b), so it never sits on the going-in sheet; not built yet
A factor on the sheet is a hypothesis about a driver, not an explanation. Nothing here has been tested for effect."""

